    "description": "The ReportingService creates relational work for several deployments. It depends only on DbConnection, DbCommand, and DbParameter interfaces, while PostgreSQL and MySQL implementations provide mutually compatible concrete classes. A report operation must obtain all three objects from the same provider configuration; mixing a PostgreSQL connection with MySQL command classes currently fails later during parameter binding. The application composition root reads a deployment key and registers the corresponding provider set. Report code must contain no provider conditionals or concrete class names, and adding an Oracle deployment should require registering one new provider set rather than editing ReportController, BillingExporter, or ScheduledReportJob. Each provider must also be able to reject unsupported products or connections cleanly. The key decision is where the contract for creating this matched, mutually compatible set of database products lives and how the deployment selects one set while keeping concrete classes out of clients.",
    "decision_statement": "Choose one creation contract that produces a matched connection, command, and parameter set from a deployment-selected provider without exposing concrete database classes to clients.",
    "notes": "abstract-factory fits the deployment-selected matched connection/command/parameter set with no provider conditionals in report code; factory-method is the near miss for single-product creation."
  },
